.TH "libnvme" 9 "enum nvme_lba_status_lbars" "October 2026" "API Manual" LINUX
.SH NAME
enum nvme_lba_status_lbars \- LBA Range Status (LBARS), used with the &struct nvme_lba_status_desc.status field.
.SH SYNOPSIS
enum nvme_lba_status_lbars {
.br
.BI "    NVME_LBA_STATUS_LBARS_SHIFT"
, 
.br
.br
.BI "    NVME_LBA_STATUS_LBARS_MASK"
, 
.br
.br
.BI "    NVME_LBA_STATUS_LBARS_MAY_ERR"
, 
.br
.br
.BI "    NVME_LBA_STATUS_LBARS_ERR"
, 
.br
.br
.BI "    NVME_LBA_STATUS_LBARS_ALLOCATED"
, 
.br
.br
.BI "    NVME_LBA_STATUS_LBARS_WRITE_UNC"

};
.SH Constants
.IP "NVME_LBA_STATUS_LBARS_SHIFT" 12
Shift amount to get the value of LBARS
.IP "NVME_LBA_STATUS_LBARS_MASK" 12
Mask to get the value of LBARS
.IP "NVME_LBA_STATUS_LBARS_MAY_ERR" 12
Each logical block may report Unrecovered
Read Error status, be a logical block
most recently written by a Write
Uncorrectable command, or be read
successfully. Used with ATYPE 10h/11h.
.IP "NVME_LBA_STATUS_LBARS_ERR" 12
Each logical block may report
Unrecovered Read Error status or be a
logical block most recently written by
a Write Uncorrectable command. Used
with ATYPE 10h/11h.
.IP "NVME_LBA_STATUS_LBARS_ALLOCATED" 12
One or more of the reported logical
blocks are allocated. Used with
ATYPE 02h.
.IP "NVME_LBA_STATUS_LBARS_WRITE_UNC" 12
Each logical block was most recently
written by a Write Uncorrectable
command. Used with ATYPE 10h/11h.
